Odysseus sat on the island suffering and grieving and turning away his face from the words of Calypso and from her charms, yearning to see his village again and smoke rising up from it. And if he had not [received] assistance from Heaven, [he could not have returned] to his village. (Homer, Odyssey 1.48-1.59)

